! FULL MAM microphysics cluster test: setsox -> gasaerexch -> rename -> apply ->
! newnuc -> coag, the CCPP equivalent of CAM's gas_phase_chemdr ->
! aero_model_gasaerexch. This is the end-to-end assembly: only true cluster
! EXTERNALS come from the snapshot; everything the cluster produces internally
! (the setsox tendency, del_h2so4_aeruptk, the vmr chain, the constituent
! tendencies) is computed in-suite.
!
! the unified snapshot captures the following sequence
!   (upstream imp_sol)
!   ------ P-1 ---------- (aerochem_vmr_presetsox_* + base oxidants,
!                          before tape)             <-- this test starts HERE
!   setsox
!   ------ P_start ------ (aerochem_vmr_* before tape)
!   gasaerexch
!   rename
!   apply tendencies from gasaerexch+rename on vmr; recover del_h2so4_aeruptk
!   ------ P_end ------- (aerochem_vmr_* after tape)
!   newnuc
!   ------ P2 ------ (aerochem_vmr_postnewnuc_* after tape)
!   coag
!   ------ P3 ------ (aerochem_vmr_postcoag_* after tape)
!   (downstream NH3 conservation)
!
! Unlike the newnuc_coag testmod, TWO tapes are used:
!  - input (ncdata) = the "before" tape:
!    mam_vmr_inject_presetsox initializes the working vmr from the P-1 (pre-setsox)
!    capture point, and the entry checkpoint saves that state so the
!    difference unpack carries the FULL setsox->coag tendency.
!
!    Quantities external to the microphysics block come from the same tape:
!      the pre-setsox oxidants,
!      mam_del_h2so4_gasprod (from gas-phase chemistry),
!      dgnum/dgnumwet/wetdens (computed by the aerosol_wet_processes, in snapshot),
!      and the newnuc met fields (zm, pblh, cld, Q).
!
!    mam_setsox_vmr_tend (rename's continuous-growth "other" tendency)
!    is computed in-suite by mam_setsox_tendency, not taken from the snapshot.
!
!    NOTE: mam_del_h2so4_aeruptk on the before tape is all zeros by construction
!    (the value does not exist yet; CAM computes it within this suite.);
!    the suite computes it in mam_vmr_apply, overwriting the read.
!
!  - results (ncdata_check) = the "after" tape, three b4b gates:
!    (1) mam_vmr_postnewnuc vs aerochem_vmr_postnewnuc_*: certifies the whole
!        setsox -> gasaerexch -> rename -> apply -> newnuc block;
!    (2) mam_vmr_postcoag vs aerochem_vmr_postcoag_*: adds the coag chaining;
!    (3) the computed del_h2so4_aeruptk vs the after tape's captured
!        mam_del_h2so4_aeruptk (reported under its standard name,
!        change_in_h2so4_molar_mixing_ratio_due_to_aerosol_uptake).
!
!    Cloud-borne aerochem_vmr_*_c* rows are kept as additional verification:
!    newnuc/coag never touch cloud-borne, so the working vmr's _c* slices must
!    stay bitwise at their P_end values (which now include setsox's aqueous
!    so4_c* production and rename's cloud-borne merge).
!
! The full bit-for-bitness of each individual scheme can be captured in a dropsonde
! run which verifies the inputs and outputs of each scheme.
! The snapshots outlined here are the result of that verification.
! Please see the suite_modal_aero_microphysics.xml header (atmospheric_physics)
! for the scheme-level detail.

